 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** $O(1)$ per query, but with a significantly higher constant factor than trilinear due to 64 coefficients (or 8 corners with gradients) and cubic polynomial evaluations [S1].
-- **Memory Complexity:** Requires storage of gradients, increasing memory usage by a factor of 4 per voxel (value + 3 gradient components) compared to value-only storage [S2, unofficial].
-- **Performance:** Slower than trilinear. Studies confirm longer processing times for upsampled 3D volumes [S1].
-- **Strengths:** $C^1$ continuity, reduced artifacts in gradient-sensitive tasks, higher accuracy $O(h^4)$ for smooth functions [S1].
-- **Limitations:** Higher computational cost, requires gradient data, potential for oscillations if data is not smooth [S1].
+*   **Time Complexity:** $O(1)$ per query, but with a large constant factor due to 64 points and cubic evaluations.
+*   **Memory Complexity:** Requires storing gradients in addition to values, doubling the memory footprint compared to scalar-only grids.
+*   **Measured Performance:** Studies confirm tricubic's edge in accuracy over trilinear for upsampled 3D volumes, albeit with longer processing times [S1].
+*   **Strengths:** $C^1$ continuity, $O(h^4)$ accuracy, reduced artifacts in gradient-sensitive tasks [S1].
+*   **Limitations:** Increased computational expense, requires gradient data [S1].
+*   **When to use:** When $C^1$ continuity is needed for differentiable outputs in visualization [S1].
+*   **When not to use:** When performance is critical and $C^0$ continuity is sufficient (use trilinear) [S1].
 
 ## Background
-Tricubic interpolation, specifically the Hermite variant, was discussed in the context of Irradiance Volumes for Games at GDC 2005 [S2, unofficial]. It is used in medical imaging and visualization where smooth, differentiable outputs are required [S1].
+Tricubic interpolation is a higher-order alternative to trilinear interpolation [S1]. It is used in medical imaging upsampling and volume rendering [S1]. The method is based on cubic Hermite patches [S2, unofficial].
 
